      {
        "review_id": 491970408,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r491970408-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Experience but be aware....",
        "text": "We visited as a group of 4 from UK.  Wow what an experience and so glad we did it, by our pockets were rung dry so be prepared!! (Backpackers on budgets)\nThe actual experience was great and insightful with a new understating of the Hindu belief and culture.\nEntrance as 1000rupee each, we then were given a guided tour which what what we assume the 1000 each was for.  Turned out not and has a very awkward experience although learnt alot from the guide.  We offered a 2000 tip to which he refused and demanded the cost as minim 4000 usually getting 8000rupee a tour.   Hard to believe.  This is after our photo with the Sadhu men and told to pay them 1000 each!! I don't believe any of this excessive amount was required but trying not to pay it was resulting in a very tense atmosphere.  All in all be prepared to pay a minimum of 3000rupee per person.  \nA very educational trip and glad we did it\n  Seeing all the offerings of animals was amazing.  You have to go if ever in Kathmandu.\n\nHope this helps prepare any other westerners visiting as we were not prepared enough money wise! \n\nX\n\n",
