      {
        "review_id": 490283286,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r490283286-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Of monkeys, Holy men, and cremations",
        "text": "Our Kathmandu day tour took us here (and it is my second time, as it's pretty much in all the tours).  It can be confronting for westerners.  There are a lot of people here(excluding the tourist contingent), poverty, beggars with deformed and missing limbs, and cremations in full view.  It's just the way life is here.\nMonkeys play in the Bagmati River below the cremations, and the ashes are simply shovelled into the river to make way for the next one, adding to the polluted state of the river.\nThere are Sadhu here (Holy Men), who will pose for photo provided they are paid, though one guide told me that they are fakes (frauds dressing up for the tourists to get money for the photos), but I don't really know either way.\nHold on and go and experience it - it's nothing you'll have seen before in western countries.",
